{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And she is left.</b> The meaning: the fortified cities of Judah will be captured, and nothing will be left except Zion." "<b>Like a hut in a vineyard.</b> The place of the watchman, and the meaning refers to the Shekhinah." "<b>Like a lodge.</b> A place for the watchman to sleep in the cucumber field." "<b>Like a besieged city.</b> Devastated, as in ובנצורים ילינו (Isaiah 65:4)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:23.498102168Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}